The page container is signed under the app's bundle identifier, not tolkara.page-container.

A player's free Apple Account build (iPhone 14 Pro Max, iOS 27.0.1, 2026-11-15) installed and
opened, and the game stopped at "container dlopen failed: ... code signature invalid ...
(errno=1)": the kernel refused the container's signature (fcntl F_ADDFILESIGS_RETURN). A free
account's provisioning profile carries LocalProvision, and with one of those iOS's libmis
accepts code outside the app (a path with no .app in it) only when <team>.<signing identifier>
matches the profile's application-identifier; otherwise it logs "Local Profile ... has
non-matching application-identifier" and the profile does not count. A paid team's profile has
no such check, which is why every device run before this passed. --identifier now defaults to
TOLKARA_BUNDLE_ID (local.tolkara.app without one, as tools/generate.sh has it), so
tools/install.sh, the probes and a run by hand all sign with it. The app signs its own
containers the same way (pocket/launcher/Pocket/PocketLocalSigning.m).
Upstream candidate: Tolkara's Local signing fails the same way for any free team.

